    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Utz’s core branded salty snacks are sustaining momentum with a ninth straight quarter of expansion, outpacing the broader category without resorting to the price cuts that larger competitors are now deploying. The portfolio’s heavy branded mix supports pricing discipline and margin gains, while demand appears resilient even against a backdrop of consumer caution. The company is gaining competitive ground as PepsiCo slashes prices and restructures, positioning Utz as the steadier, focused snacking pure-play.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership reaffirmed full-year guidance after the solid quarter, signaling confidence and operational visibility. The team is driving cash-flow improvements while absorbing cost pressures, keeping the focus on organic branded growth rather than chasing volume through discounting. After a prolonged share-price decline that reflected deep market skepticism, this delivery—coupled with maintained guidance—begins to rebuild management credibility and suggests execution is on track.",
